# Build context exclusions for backend/Dockerfile.
#
# The context is backend/ (see docker-compose.yml). Everything listed here is
# either large, irrelevant to the image, or must never reach a layer.
#
# The `.env` exclusion is a SECURITY control, not a size optimisation
# (brief §18 "do not hard-code secrets" / "avoid exposing credentials";
# CONTRACT §0.2). The backend reads DEEPSEEK_API_KEY from backend/.env. A build
# context that includes it would copy it into a layer, and a layer is a
# published artefact: `docker history` and `docker save` would expose the key to
# anyone who can pull the image, even if a later layer deleted the file.
# Keep this line.

# --- secrets and local configuration ---------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# --- local environment and caches ------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/

# --- runtime state ----------------------------------------------------------
# The SQLite database and anything else written at runtime. Created inside the
# image by the Dockerfile; never copied in. A baked-in database would ship one
# machine's local state as another's starting point.
data/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.log
logs/

# --- not needed to build or run --------------------------------------------
tests/
loadtest/
docs/
.github/
CONTRACT.md
README.md
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
docker-compose*.yml
Makefile
*.http

# --- scratch / throwaway -----------------------------------------------------
# A tracked capacity-probe script (backend/probe_sim.py) was removed from the
# repository; no scratch or benchmark file belongs in a build context either.
# See docs/hygiene.md.
probe_*.py
bench_*.py
scratch/
